# The default location the worktree tooling stands isolation checkouts up in, so
# it recurs rather than happening once. A linked worktree carries a `.git`
# pointer *file*, whose kind no ruling in tools/vos/checks/marks.py covers, and
# the selftest's sandbox reads untracked files where check.py reads the git
# index: the checker stays green and the selftest's baseline goes red, which
# stops every mutant from deciding anything. Ignored here rather than refused as
# a tree, so that anything else unruled landing under `.claude/` is still loud.
.claude/worktrees/

# The generated reading view tools/read-view.py rebuilds on demand: a derived
# artifact of the two documents and never a source, kept out of the index and,
# being ignored, out of the selftest sandbox's corpus alike. Anchored to the
# root on purpose: an unanchored out/ would silently swallow any out directory
# a future vendored tree carries, and a curation batch adds by recursive add.
/out/

# Where the freeze's producers write what §4 joins, on `/out/`'s exact precedent and
# for its exact reasons. An image built under the provisional profile is a measurement
# artifact and is neither deployed nor stored (R-18-003c), so it is derived output and
# never a source; and keeping it out of the index keeps it out of the selftest
# sandbox's corpus too, where an untracked file under a directory no rule opens would
# leave check.py green and the selftest's baseline red. Anchored to the root on the
# same ground `/out/` is: an unanchored build/ would swallow any build directory a
# future vendored tree carries.
/build/

proofs/*.vo
proofs/*.vok
proofs/*.vos
proofs/*.glob
proofs/.*.aux
__pycache__/
